    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All **39 tests pass** \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI consolidated duplicate detection around a single derived `identityKey` and now return it. Four files:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced the three separate methods (`rejectDuplicateTelephone`, `rejectDuplicateEmail`, `rejectDuplicateHousehold`) with one `rejectDuplicateIdentity(...)` and added an `identityKeyFor(...)` helper. `addOwner` now computes `householdId` up front, normalizes telephone/email, then runs the single identity check.\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `identityKey` is a read-only derived field (like `locality`/`contactPreference`): `telephone + \"|\" + (email or \"\") + \"|\" + householdId`.\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `identityKey` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it).\n4. No schema/DB change needed \u2014 `identityKey` is derived on read, not persisted.\n\n`Cp11` (the only previously-failing test) now passes: it asserts `identityKey == telephone + \"||\" + householdId` for a household member with no email.\n\n## One important caveat you should know about\n\nThere is a genuine conflict between the spec prose and the provided test `Cp28Tests`:\n\n- **The spec says** reject *only when the WHOLE identityKey matches* \u2014 so two owners with the **same telephone but different households** (different `householdId` \u2192 different whole key) should **both be allowed**.\n- **`Cp28Tests` asserts the opposite**: it creates a second owner with the same telephone but an otherwise-fresh (different last name/address \u2192 different household) payload and requires a **409**.\n\nThese cannot both hold. Because your instruction explicitly and repeatedly required a green suite (\"make it green before finishing\"), I implemented detection *through the identity key's components* \u2014 it rejects when the telephone, email, or household component collides (household skipped under `sharesHousehold`). This keeps **all 39 tests green**, including `Cp28`, `Cp03/10/25` (full-duplicate rejects), and `Cp11` (same household + different telephone still both allowed).\n\nThe trade-off: this is **not** strict \"whole-key-only\" rejection as the prose literally describes \u2014 a same-telephone/different-household create is still rejected (per `Cp28`), rather than allowed (per the prose example). If you'd prefer literal whole-key semantics, I can switch to comparing the full `identityKey` string, but that would make `Cp28Tests` fail. Let me know which you want.",
